    <section class="scroll-snap-card" id="projects">
        <h1>my projects</h1>
        <section class="project-card">
            <div class="project-image">
                <img src="/assets/cellmace.png" />
            </div>
            <article>
                <h2>cellmaCE</h2>
                <p>
                    cellmaCE is a
                    <a href="https://samhogan.itch.io/cell-machine"
                        >cell machine</a
                    >
                    mod for the TI-84 Plus CE calculator. cell machine and its
                    mods used to be one of my passions when the fandom was much
                    more alive in early 2020s. this tribute brings the game with
                    its base cells and accurate simulation to the classroom for
                    when you're bored. it features an easy to use editor and 10
                    save slots to show off your contraptions.
                    <a href="https://github.com/mstfbil/cellmace"
                        >here is the repo.</a
                    >
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>
        <section class="project-card">
            <div class="project-image">
                <img src="/assets/the_passing_of_midnight.png" />
            </div>
            <article>
                <h2>The Passing of Midnight</h2>
                <p>
                    <i>The Passing of Midnight</i> was my entry to
                    <a href="https://itch.io/jam/gmtk-jam-2026"
                        >GMTK Game Jam 2026</a
                    >. you are kidnapped and put in a mysterious room with
                    nothing but an old clock in it. you're supposed to nudge the
                    clock in the right ways to only delay the inevitable.
                    <a href="https://voltie-dev.itch.io/the-passing-of-midnight"
                        >play on itch.io</a
                    >.
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>
        <section class="project-card">
            <div class="project-image">
                <img src="/assets/lipuce.png" />
            </div>
            <article>
                <h2>lipuCE</h2>
                <p>
                    lipuCE is a toki pona dictionary that runs on TI-84 Plus CE.
                    it includes all the core words and has releases that include
                    up to obscure words. you can view word definitions.
                    <a href="http://ceme.tech/DL3103"
                        >you can download it from here.</a
                    >
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>
        <section class="project-card">
            <div class="project-image">
                <img src="/assets/arrayshift.png" />
            </div>
            <article>
                <h2>arrayshift();</h2>
                <p>
                    <i>arrayshift();</i> was my entry to
                    <a href="https://itch.io/jam/gmtk-2025"
                        >GMTK Game Jam 2025</a
                    >. this game might seem like a simple maze at first glance,
                    however you quickly find out that your path is blocked.
                    you'll need to manipulate the very map to win.
                    <a href="https://voltie-dev.itch.io/arrayshift"
                        >click here to play!</a
                    >
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>
    </section>
    <section class="scroll-snap-card" id="latest-posts">
        <section class="card">
            <h1>latest posts from my blog</h1>
            <ul style="list-style: none;">
            {% for post in collections.posts reversed %}
                <li>
                    <a href="{{ post.url }}">
                        <b>{{ post.date | date: "%B %d, %y" }}</b> - {{ post.data.title }}
                    </a>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
            <a href="/blog">see more...</a>
        </ul>
        </section>
    </section>
